  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.29 Graffiti remover",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.29 “Graffiti remover” means a product labeled to remove spray paint, ink, marker, crayon, lipstick, nail polish, or shoe polish, from a variety of non-cloth or nonfabric substrates. The term includes products labeled for dual use as both a paint stripper and graffiti remover. The term does not include paint remover or stripper, nail polish remover, or spot remover.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
